<!--
  Which Bracha?  (Playtime613 game id: brachos)  v1
  Food rides along the Shabbos table; tap the right bracha rishona.
  ===== FOOD LIST FOR RABBINIC CHECK (Ashkenazi minhag; only clear-cut, everyday cases) =====
  HAMOTZI   : challah, bagel, pitta, bread (slice/loaf), bread roll
  MEZONOS   : cake, chocolate-chip cookie, spaghetti, pretzel (hard, flour), rugelach
  HAGAFEN   : grape juice, kiddush wine
  HA'EITZ   : apple, orange, pear, peach, plum, cherries, dates, whole grapes (tricky: vs Hagafen)
  HA'ADAMAH : baked potato, carrot, cucumber, tomato, corn on the cob, watermelon,
              banana (tricky; reason shown: "The banana plant grows a new stem every year, so it's not a tree"),
              strawberries (tricky), peanuts (tricky)
  SHEHAKOL  : water, milk, egg (boiled), chicken, fish, cheese, lollipop, chocolate bar (tricky),
              soda, ice lolly, mushroom (tricky)
  Deliberately LEFT OUT (machlokes / depends on preparation or amount): rice, cornflakes, oatmeal,
  granola, popcorn, applesauce, fruit juices other than grape, smoothies, potato chips, crackers,
  matzah, donuts, pizza, quinoa, sushi, pineapple, olives, raw potato, leafy greens, anything
  chocolate-covered or mixed.
  Wrong-answer reason lines are in the FOODS table below (one per food).
  Levels: 1 Hamotzi/Ha'eitz/Shehakol (4 each) - 2 adds Ha'adamah - 3 all six - 4 faster + tricky - 5 challenge mix.
  Website taster: levels 1-2 need nothing but this file; if window.PT613_UNLOCKED===false, levels 3-5 show a padlock.
  Offline only. localStorage: pt613_tut_brachos (tour offer), pt613_music_brachos, pt613_sfx_brachos, pt613_best_brachos.
-->
